I can help you get organized. Below are focused questions to ask Michael Torres, plus an evidence checklist and quick next-step recommendations so you’re ready for the preliminary hearing and possible trial.

First — one quick clarification for me: when you say “my status has changed,” what changed specifically (moved, job/income change, health, bankruptcy, incarceration, change in tenancy, etc.)? That will change which questions are most important.

Suggested questions to ask your lawyer (grouped by priority)

Immediate / before the preliminary hearing
- Given my changed status (explain change), how does that affect our case strategy and what I must disclose to the court?
- Do we need any additional evidence before the next court date? If so, which items are highest priority?
- Are there any deadlines coming up (discovery, motions, exhibit exchange, witness lists) that I need to meet before the hearing?
- Should we ask the court for a continuance to get more evidence or witnesses if needed? What is the process and likelihood of approval?
- Can the preliminary hearing result in a final ruling, or is it limited to case management/pretrial matters in this court?
- Do you recommend mediation or settlement discussions before the hearing? If yes, how should I prepare for that?

Evidence / documents and proof
- Which documents will be admissible and most persuasive for my defense (lease, rent ledger, payment receipts, bank statements, texts/emails)?
- Do we need sworn statements or affidavits from witnesses? Should they come to the preliminary hearing, or can we submit written statements?
- Do we need subpoenas for any records (bank, phone, landlord’s records)? If so, when should we request them?
- Are photographs, videos, repair invoices, and inspection reports sufficient to support habitability/repair claims or counterclaims?
- Will hearsay (e.g., secondhand statements) be a problem for any evidence I have?

Case specifics and legal strategy
- Do we have grounds for counterclaims (wrongful eviction, failure to maintain premises, illegal fees, security deposit issues, harassment, etc.)?
- What defenses do you consider strongest, and what evidence specifically supports each?
- Based on your experience in Maricopa County, what common objections or evidentiary problems should I anticipate?
- How should we handle communications with the opposing party/creditor going forward (what to say in writing vs. avoid)?
- If I’ve moved or changed contact info, how do we ensure I still receive court notices and service properly?

Practical trial prep
- How should I prepare my witness(es) to testify? What practice or script would help them be concise and credible?
- How many copies of exhibits do I need to bring to the hearing/trial and in what format (paper, photo, electronic)?
- Do we need demonstrative aids (timeline, spreadsheet) for the judge? Can you help assemble them?
- What is the expected timeline from preliminary hearing to trial if the case isn’t resolved?

Financial and outcome questions
- What are the possible outcomes (judgment amount, possession order, cost/attorney fees) we should prepare for?
- If the creditor obtains a judgment, what are the enforcement methods in Arizona and how might they affect me?
- If my income/status has changed (e.g., lost job, filed bankruptcy), how will that affect collection or the court’s approach?

Administrative / communication
- What do you need from me before the next hearing and by when?
- Can you confirm the date/time/location of the next hearing and any documents I must bring?
- How do you prefer I send documents to you (secure email, portal, in person) and what naming/organization will help you most?
- If I want you to request a continuance or file a motion, can you do that and what do you need from me to proceed?

Evidence checklist — gather and organize these now
- Lease/rental agreement and any amendments
- Rent payment history: receipts, bank statements, canceled checks
- Landlord’s rent ledger, demand letters, notice to pay or vacate, eviction notices
- All written communications: emails, texts, messaging app screenshots (show timestamps, sender/recipient)
- Notices received from court or opposing counsel (dates and proof of service)
- Photographs/videos of unit condition, damages, repairs (dated)
- Repair estimates/invoices, receipts for repairs you paid for
- Move-in/move-out condition reports, security deposit documentation
- Witness contact info and short written statements (dates, what they saw/heard)
- Any police reports, code violation notices, housing inspection reports
- Proof of payments to third parties (utilities, HOA) if relevant
- Bank statements showing deposits/withdrawals tied to rent or payments
- Any settlement offers, payment plans, or prior agreements

How to prepare those items
- Create a single chronological timeline (one page) of key events (dates of lease, payments, notices, communications, repairs, hearings).
- Label exhibit files clearly (E.g., EX1 Lease, EX2 Payment ledger, EX3 Texts 01-17-2026).
- Make one binder or folder with originals and a second with copies for the court and opposing counsel.
- Scan documents into PDF and keep a backup copy (USB/cloud). Bring printed copies to the hearing.

Tactical points to ask your lawyer
- Should we file any pretrial motions (to exclude evidence, compel documents, protective orders)?
- Is there anything I should stop doing now (e.g., direct communications with the creditor) to avoid harming the case?
- If my status change affects finances, should I propose a payment plan or loss mitigation to the creditor now or wait?
- If the creditor is not the original landlord (assigned debt), should we challenge their standing or chain of title?

Sample short email you can send Michael (I can draft/send if you want)
Subject: Questions & Documents before preliminary hearing — [Your Name] — Maricopa County

Hi Michael — quick list of questions and items I can bring before the preliminary hearing:
1) Does my recent status change (explain change in 1 sentence) change strategy or evidence needs?  
2) What exact documents do you want before [date]? (Lease, payment records, texts, photos, witness statements, etc.)  
3) Should we request a continuance to gather more evidence?  
4) Any other immediate steps I should take or stop taking?

I can bring a timeline and scanned copies of the items below — please confirm which you need first:
- Lease, rent ledger, bank statements, payment receipts, texts/emails, photos, repair invoices, notice(s), witness names.

Thanks — please let me know what you need by [give a date 3–7 days before the hearing].

Would you like me to:
- Draft the exact email to Michael for you to review and send?
- Help draft the one-page timeline and label exhibits based on your documents?
- Or tailor the questions if you tell me what “status changed” means?

If you want, tell me the exact status change now and I’ll customize the question list to that situation.

