Hi Michael — I have a preliminary hearing coming up and want to be fully prepared. A few quick questions:
1) What is the purpose of the upcoming hearing (scheduling/settlement/evidentiary)?  
2) Are there discovery or exhibit deadlines I should be aware of?  
3) Which documents or subpoenas should I prioritize obtaining before the hearing?  
4) If we can’t get key evidence by the date, should we seek a continuance and on what grounds?  
I can gather the following immediately: lease, payment records, texts/emails, photos, and witness contact info. Would you like me to compile these into an indexed packet and send them to you?  
Thanks — [Your name]

Next step from me
- I can: a) draft a full email to Michael including the checklist and timeline; b) draft a one-page exhibit index and timeline template for you to fill in; or c) walk through the items you already have and identify gaps. Which would you like?

If you answer the two clarifying questions (what changed about your status and the hearing date/type), I’ll tailor the checklist and draft an email you can send or I can send it for you.

