2) Do we need subpoenas or witness affidavits? If yes, who should we subpoena and by when?
3) Do you want originals or are copies sufficient?
4) When do you need the final exhibit packet from me?
I’m available to meet/call this week. Thanks, [Your name / best contact number]

9) Final practical tips
- Do not delete any evidence — even messages you think are irrelevant.
- Keep a single master folder (physical + digital) and update it only by adding new documents.
- Ask Michael for a prioritized “must-have” list so you don’t spend time on low-value docs.
- If money is an issue for subpoenas or experts, ask Michael about low-cost alternatives (affidavits, public records requests, court clerks’ guidance).
- Ask Michael about local Maricopa County small-claims/justice court procedures or a court self-help resource link if you want to confirm filing/format rules.

